CRITERION_10_FINAL=CLOSED per the completion criterion's own wording (two independent security reviews both PASS), decided by the user on 2026-08-06 (route 乙). Route 1 (cursor-agent, comprehensive) and route 2 (Hermes, security boundary) both returned PASS against identity c1f7c91b… with zero BLOCKING, each independently recomputing the identity and confirming a zero-change workspace. Route 3 (evidence authenticity / false-green detection) ran three times without ever producing a PASS-shaped verdict: round 1 died on HTTP 429 upstream rate limiting after 620s (its seven mandatory checks had actually completed in-process but were never summarised), round 2 returned one BLOCKING, round 2b returned two. All three BLOCKING items were main-agent prose errors while maintaining this very sidecar — none pointed at a product defect. Because the review object includes the record of the review itself, every prose fix moved the workspace identity and demanded another round; the loop consumed seven identities and four dispatches. The user's ruling: stop the loop, do not block criterion #12, and record the missing third verdict as an administrative remainder. WHAT WAS NOT OBTAINED, stated plainly: no third party has signed PASS on the claim that this freeze evidence is internally consistent as prose. The residual risk is documentation-layer, not code or artifact layer. The untaken root fix is to move all narrative text out to a separate .r6-review-log.md and keep this sidecar to machine-checkable key/value pairs only.
ROUND_2B_BLOCKING_RESOLVED=The round-2b route returned BLOCKING on two items, both VALID and both main-agent prose errors rather than product defects. B2: this sidecar, docs/R6-0.4.0-验收报告.md and HANDOVER.md each described "the round-2b identity" with the literal prefix f988baea…, which had already been superseded by a later stage of the same round — the hash was written into prose and then the SHA changed underneath it. B3: ROUND_2_IDENTITY_NOTE still spoke in the present tense ("This is the round-2 identity… five gates read 318") after the workspace had moved to 293 files and FIVE_GATES=319. Fixes: no prose anywhere now embeds a literal hash for the current identity — all such references point at the R6_TECHNICAL_CANDIDATE_SHA256 header field; ROUND_2_IDENTITY_NOTE and SUPERSEDES were merged into a single strictly past-tense IDENTITY_HISTORY listing all six superseded identities with the readings each carried. Also cross-checked at round-2b's request: the two ledgers legitimately differ in cardinality (R5_ADDED_PATHS 64 vs _R5_PLANNING_DELTA_PATHS 62) because ADDED additionally carries the four dist/ 0.4.0 artifacts while DELTA additionally carries two R5 planning docs; all five review-related briefs are declared in BOTH ledgers, so there is no missing-declaration defect.
SIX_GATES_PLUS_K2=403 passed, 0 failed (33.69s) — five gates + tests/test_reproducible_release.py; K2 re-run because this round edited docs/R6-0.4.0-验收报告.md, from which K2 regex-extracts the plugin ZIP hash line.
ROUND_2_BLOCKING_RESOLVED=The round-2 evidence-authenticity route (cursor-agent) returned BLOCKING on exactly one item and it was VALID: this sidecar still read FULL_NOBUILD_PYTEST=1585 while the round-2 identity independently measures 1586. Root cause was a main-agent omission — FIVE_GATES was updated 317->318 for the round-2 brief but the full-run figure was not updated in the same pass, even though 1586 had already been measured and written into the round-2 brief's expected baseline. Fixed in two stages. Stage 1 (292 files): FULL_NOBUILD_PYTEST corrected 1585->1586, propagated to docs/R6-0.4.0-验收报告.md and HANDOVER.md; .r6-final-review-task.md keeps its round-1 baseline (1585/317, historically correct) under an explicit superseded banner; five gates + K2 re-ran 402 passed / 0 failed. Stage 2 (293 files, the current identity recorded in R6_TECHNICAL_CANDIDATE_SHA256 above): the round-2b confirmation brief .r6-round2b-blocking-fix-verify-task.md was added and declared in both ledgers, moving the figures to 1587 / 319 — both measured and written together this time, which is the actual fix for the omission pattern. See IDENTITY_HISTORY for the full chain of superseded identities. NOTE ON THIS FIELD: prose in this sidecar must never embed a literal hash for "the current identity" — that is exactly how round-2b's B2 arose. Always point at the R6_TECHNICAL_CANDIDATE_SHA256 header field instead; only IDENTITY_HISTORY carries literal hashes, and every entry there is explicitly past-tense.
IDENTITY_HISTORY=Past identities only, all past-tense; the live value is always R6_TECHNICAL_CANDIDATE_SHA256 in the header. (1) c1f7c91b164dcab4aa89e8da5cf4da8baf5f83bec3c9dd9092d522ffb7978766, 291 files / 30161 bytes — the round-1 review identity. Route 1 (cursor-agent, comprehensive) and route 2 (Hermes, security boundary) both returned PASS against this snapshot and those verdicts remain valid for it. Readings were 1585 / 317. (2) 744334001c606cf020eb57fd7e9355e406a5c6e76bf894179cbfa5dcea32ed54, 291 files / 30161 bytes — existed only between the round-1 doc backfill and the round-2 banner added to .r6-final-review-task.md; never bound to any review. (3) 555a253780e18e76f063c4699845ef099ff6d227121423b50d6fab5a27d4c5e1, 291 files / 30161 bytes — likewise transient, never reviewed. (4) f204b64fb808243c90fdec173ee5443c2120ed9a46c3fc7acca75e85e862f12a, 292 files / 30273 bytes — the round-2 review identity, differing from round 1 by exactly one added file (.r6-round2-evidence-authenticity-task.md, declared in both ledgers), which is why readings were 1586 / 318. The round-2 evidence-authenticity route reviewed this snapshot and returned BLOCKING on one valid item (see ROUND_2_BLOCKING_RESOLVED). (5) c30051ed76e73af3270a83b71837095eedf6fd820c06994e92c4149fa8140525, 292 files / 30273 bytes — stage-1 fix of that BLOCKING; never independently reviewed. (6) f988baea8cd5489a635ecce1516f83c9bddf50c424930c55266c98b64a5fbd42, 293 files / 30383 bytes — stage-2 after adding the round-2b brief; superseded within the same round by adding the measured SIX_GATES_PLUS_K2 figure. (7) c5546c562f3d99497943d9fd2f7bcc04659d2ca5356c280ec9ac9b1e765da3a5, 293 files / 30383 bytes — the round-2b review identity; the round-2b route reviewed this snapshot and returned BLOCKING on two valid prose items (see ROUND_2B_BLOCKING_RESOLVED). (8) ed63a1fe7ef3d697bd900aa4b4e6455fa8648def74f771f1150e1b81f432683c, 293 files / 30383 bytes — the B2/B3 prose fixes; superseded by the criterion-10 closing backfill (report/HANDOVER/CLAUDE status lines plus the append to .r5-tdd-evidence.log), which produced the identity now in the header. Throughout this chain no production code changed: the deltas are documentation backfill, review briefs, and their ledger declarations.
