CRITERION_10_ROUND_1=Three routes dispatched 2026-08-06 against identity c1f7c91b… (291/30161). Route 1 cursor-agent (proc_6775e8622f2a): PASS, nine aspects, zero BLOCKING. Route 2 Hermes security-boundary subagent: PASS, aspects 1-8, zero BLOCKING, independently located the root cause of both caliber deviations above. Route 3 Hermes evidence-authenticity subagent: NO VERDICT — died at 620s on HTTP 429 upstream rate limiting plus iteration-budget exhaustion (same failure mode as the R5 round). All three independently recomputed the identity and got 291/30161/c1f7c91b… with MATCHES_SIDECAR=True; all three confirmed zero repo mutation.
CRITERION_10_ROUND_1_GAP=Route 3 completed all seven of its assigned checks in-flight but never emitted a report. The main agent independently re-ran its core verification: ledger cardinalities 62/25/2/44 all non-empty (vacuous-green risk excluded) and five negative cases via parameter injection — unregistered file RED, de-register backfill RED, de-register sidecar RED, declared-added file missing RED, deleted module resurrected RED, healthy control GREEN. That proves the ledger registration is load-bearing classification rather than a loosened gate. Round 2 of route 3 is being re-dispatched on a different kernel to obtain a formal third verdict.
CRITERION_10_STATUS=NOT executed for 0.4.0. The R5 three-way final review bound the R5 candidate identity (270 files / 27928 bytes / c8a60656fa397c26e65137ba20e64d05ee5ad6ea02b9ffd207a59fad50eb17d8). R6's five slices drifted the workspace, so that review does not cover the 0.4.0 release. grep of .r5-tdd-evidence.log R6 section (NR>=3300) for review/终审/reviewer/independent returns zero hits. This sidecar exists to give criterion #10 an identity to bind to.
